power: supply: max77705_charger: review fixes for the OTG regulator and limits

From review of the Galaxy Tab S8+ charger bring-up:

- The CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT property clamped to 3.2 A, past both the
  battery node's constant-charge-current-max and the 6-bit CHG_CC field
  (3.2 A is code 64, which the field masks to 0). Clamp writes, and the
  probe-time setting, to the battery's maximum and 63 x 50 mA.
- Input voltage regulation is left to the hardware; clear DIS_AICL
  (CNFG_06 bit 4) at probe, as stock does, in case a factory flow set it.
- The OTG regulator's enable and disable, and the shutdown hook, did a
  read-modify-write of the mode nibble; use regmap_field_update_bits()
  so another writer of the field cannot interleave.
- Unbinding the charger left a running boost with no owner; clear the
  OTG bits in the devm disable action as well.
- A failed float-voltage write was ignored and probe succeeded with the
  float wherever it was; fail probe instead.

